  "summary": "Bind native cache entries to selected SDKs, retain the source-compilation fallback after a failed Metal toolchain probe, and prevent reference-adapter builds from rebuilding unrelated executables. Expand reset and cache regression coverage.",
  "regressions": [
    "SDK selection invalidates native compiler identity.",
    "A failed optional Metal toolchain probe consistently falls back without publishing a partial compiler identity.",
    "All adapter builds explicitly select their binary.",
    "Loaded-program reset after growth, cache artifact inventories, cached/uncached C and Metal state, initial-state changes, and A-B-A switching."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "The early integration run was interrupted for final lint and cache-probe corrections; only the completed final-source run is acceptance evidence.",
    "Strict native Clippy now boxes the Metal frame session; no physics operations change.",
    "The preflight Python handoff checks used prior-source artifacts and correctly rejected seven stale source envelopes; regenerate the full current-source matrix before acceptance.",
    "No physics tolerance or case changes."
  ]
